    "text": {
     "en": "India's neighbours include Nepal, Bhutan, Bangladesh, Sri Lanka, Pakistan, China, Myanmar and Afghanistan. India has shared trade, languages and religions with them for centuries.\nBuddhism spread from India to Sri Lanka, Nepal, Tibet, China and South-East Asia. Ancient trade routes like the Silk Road linked India to the wider world.\nToday countries cooperate on trade, rivers, travel and culture."
